---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Free Online Image Tools — Resize, Compress & Edit | ConvertAnyFile" description="Free browser-based image tools with no source-image upload. Resize and compress JPG, PNG and WebP images, remove visible watermarks, and process image batches locally.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Image Tools</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Free Online Image Tools</span><h1>Private image tools that run in your browser.</h1><p>Resize and compress everyday images, or use focused watermark-removal workflows. Working tools process source images locally in the browser and support batch-oriented downloads without a remote source-image upload queue.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Image utility preview</span><h2>Resize and compress are the next shared image workflows.</h2><p><a href="/resize-image/"><strong>Resize Image</strong></a> handles target dimensions, proportional fit and percentage scaling. <a href="/compress-image/"><strong>Compress Image</strong></a> adds output quality and format controls with before-and-after size reporting. Both reuse the existing browser-side ImageMagick worker.</p></div><ImageToolGrid /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Choose by job</span><h2>Utility transforms and focused visual editing stay separate.</h2><p>Resize and compression are deterministic transforms: add a batch, choose shared settings, process, and download. Watermark tools remain interactive because they need mask placement and per-image visual review.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Local by design</strong><p>Image decoding, resizing, recompression, mask editing, visible-pixel repair, output encoding and ZIP creation run in your browser for supported tools. The source-image workflow does not require an upload-and-wait conversion queue.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Choose the right tool</span><h2>Start with the change you actually need.</h2></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Best when</th><th>Main controls</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/resize-image/"><strong>Resize Image</strong></a></td><td>You need smaller or exact image dimensions for a site, form, profile or delivery workflow.</td><td>Width × height, keep aspect ratio, percentage</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/compress-image/"><strong>Compress Image</strong></a></td><td>You need a smaller file size while keeping useful visual quality.</td><td>Quality, Same/JPG/WebP/PNG, size comparison</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/gemini-ai-logo-remover/"><strong>Gemini Watermark Remover</strong></a></td><td>A small visible Gemini-style sparkle watermark or similar compact corner mark.</td><td>Circle, 4-Point Star</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/remove-watermark/"><strong>Remove Watermark</strong></a></td><td>The visible mark can be rectangular, round, square, diamond-shaped, sparkle-shaped or text.</td><td>Rectangle, Circle, Square, Diamond, 4-Point Star, Text</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Roadmap discipline</span><h2>New routes appear only after the browser workflow exists.</h2><p>Crop, rotate/flip, metadata, background utilities and bulk rename remain roadmap items until their processing and download behavior are implemented and tested. This keeps the Image Tools hub useful instead of filling it with placeholder SEO pages.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Shared engine, separate interaction</strong><p>Resize and Compress reuse the image worker used by converters. Stateful mask editing continues to use the dedicated Image Tools editor because its interaction model is different.</p></div></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
